# KratosOS: never install a mail transfer agent.
#
# A privacy/anti-forensics desktop has no use for a mail server, and Debian's
# default MTA (exim4) installs a SUID-root binary with a long history of root
# CVEs. It only ever arrived as a SOFT dependency (rkhunter Recommends
# default-mta / bsd-mailx), so blocking it simply leaves those Recommends
# unsatisfied. Placed in includes.chroot_before_packages so it applies while
# the image is built AND stays in the installed system (an `apt install` that
# hard-requires an MTA will now refuse instead of silently adding one; remove
# this file if you genuinely need local mail).
Package: exim4*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: postfix*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: sendmail*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
